==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|to-day||archaic}}, {{alter|en|to day||obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|2day||Internet slang|text messaging}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|today}}, {{m|enm|to-daie}}, {{m|enm|todæig}}, from {{inh|en|ang|tōdæġ}}, {{m|ang|tō dæġe|t=today|lit=on [the/this] day, [this] day forward}}, equivalent to {{af|en|to|day}}. Compare {{cog|stq|däälich|t=today}}, {{cog|nl|vandaag|t=today}}, {{cog|osx|hindag|t=today|lit=[this] day forward}}, {{cog|nds-de|vandage}}, {{m|nds-de|vandaag|t=today}}, {{cog|sv|i dag}}, {{m|sv|idag|t=today}}.

===Pronunciation===
