* {{rhymes|en|eɪ|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# On the current [[day]] or [[date]].
#: {{ux|en|I want this done '''today'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Today''', my brother went to the shops.}}
# In the current [[era]]; [[nowadays]]; [[these days]].
#: {{ux|en|In the 1500s, people had to do things by hand, but '''today''' we have electric can openers.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-06-22|volume=407|issue=8841|page=70
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21579879-buy-out-firm-really-does-focus-operational-improvements-engineers|title=Engineers of a different kind
|passage=Private-equity nabobs bristle at being dubbed mere financiers.{{...}}Much of their pleading is public-relations bluster. Clever financial ploys are what have made billionaires of the industry’s veterans. “Operational improvement” in a portfolio company has often meant little more than promising colossal bonuses to sitting chief executives if they meet ambitious growth targets. That model is still prevalent '''today'''.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130727072152/http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21579879-buy-out-firm-really-does-focus-operational-improvements-engineers}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} On the [[day]] of a [[recurring]] [[cycle]] or [[event]] which is currently happening.
#: {{ux|en|We used to prepare everything '''today''', but now we split it over two days.}}

