# The [[current]] [[day]] or [[date]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Today''' is the day we'll fix this once and for all.}}
#: {{ux|en|We could've spent '''today''' at the seaside if it weren't gusty.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1899|author=w:Hughes Mearns
|title={{w|Antigonish (poem)|Antigonish}}
|passage=Yesterday, upon the stair&nbsp;/ I met a man who wasn’t there&nbsp;/ He wasn’t there again '''today'''&nbsp;/ I wish, I wish he’d go away&nbsp;&hellip;}}
# {{lb|en|informal|or|meteorology}} The 24-[[hour]] [[period]] beginning at 5 or 6 [[a.m.]] or [[sunrise]] of the current day.
# The [[present]] [[era]]; [[nowadays]].
#: {{ux|en|This is the sporty jacket for '''today'''{{'}}s modern man on the go.}}
#: {{ux|en|The youth of '''today''' have never known what life is like without a cell phone.}}

====Usage notes====
''Todays'' is a mostly literary plural. It refers to days that we experience, have experienced or will experience as "today". More colloquial are {{m|en|these days}} and {{m|en|nowadays}}.

